    <string name="connection_waiting">Waiting for the television… If it asks to allow debugging from this computer, accept with the remote.</string>
    <string name="connection_problem_refused">Connection refused: network debugging does not seem to be enabled on the television.</string>
    <string name="connection_problem_timeout">The television did not answer in time. If it shows an authorisation request, accept it with the remote, then try again.</string>
    <string name="connection_problem_unauthorized">The television closed the connection. Accept the debugging request with the remote, ticking “Always allow from this computer”.</string>
    <string name="connection_problem_unreachable">Television unreachable: check that it is switched on and connected to the same network as this computer.</string>
    <string name="connection_problem_other">The connection failed.</string>
    <string name="connection_help_title">First time? Prepare the television</string>
    <string name="connection_help_1">1. On the television, open Settings → About (sometimes under System or Device preferences), then press OK seven times on the build number. Developer options appear.</string>
    <string name="connection_help_2">2. In Developer options, enable network debugging — depending on the television it is called “Network debugging”, “ADB debugging” or “USB debugging”.</string>
    <string name="connection_help_3">3. Come back here: the television appears in the list above within a few seconds. Otherwise, type its IP address, shown in Settings → Network.</string>
    <string name="connection_help_4">4. On the first connection, the television asks to allow debugging from this computer: accept with the remote, ticking “Always allow”. It will not ask again, even after a reboot.</string>

